  "context": "Step of the corpus rule remediation plan (crr-00-corpus-rule-remediation-plan). Plan written 2026-11-22 and reviewed twice by an independent adversarial reviewer; counts marked (R) were measured by that reviewer and must be re-measured, not trusted. Owner decisions were given by choice dialog on 2026-11-22 and are quoted in crr-00.\n\n2026-11-26 staging state: branch feat/staging-crr-b3 at 1008c6eab0 (worktree /Users/joe/Developer/BenchBox.wt-staging-crr-b3), including the label wording fix (full TPC sentence, Subscale). Not in a pull request; rebase after the corpus rule PR merges (explorer-data batch).",
  "description": "## Problem\nThe pipeline ranks every run as its own row; the meta-leaderboard keeps the best rank per variant with no version (R). Methodology answer 3 requires the median across runs with every run published.\n\n## Change (_project/scripts/explorer_pipeline/)\n- Emit, per result: class, lane, labels, score and score source from the rule; identity and comparison version; observed engine; \"row counts not checked\" and \"single iteration\" labels.\n- Per identity and cohort: one median row. As methodology answer 3 says, take the median of each query's time across the runs, then compute the lane's score from those medians; show the run count and the spread of the run-level scores. Every run stays reachable. Ranking uses median rows.\n- A partial result (power and throughput, no refresh) enters both the power-only and the throughput cohort.\n- The meta-leaderboard combines ranks of the leaderboard version only, never ranks from different versions under one label.\n- Leaderboards: per platform and variant, the newest released version that has a ranked result (owner decision 4). A version view lists all.\n- Bump the read-model version. Update browser-duckdb-schema.sql, visible_metrics.yaml and check_explorer_compat.py.\n\n## Decision gates\n- Merge only after crr-b2 is deployed. Rankings for stored results change on the public site at this step; the labels are already rendered by crr-b2. Confirm on the deployed site that a power-only TPC result shows its labels before closing; if not, revert this merge and report.\n- If a platform's rank changes by more than three places in any cohort because of the median rule, list it in the pull request body. No stop.\n\n## Guardrails (apply to every item of this plan)\n- Fix the root cause for every platform and benchmark. No rule, exception, label or test may name a platform or a version matrix. Only the pvm-p* items may name Polars, and only to run and stage that run's files.\n- Never edit a stored result file to make it pass. Outcomes change only through the rule.\n- Any change to the outcome of a stored result must show in the committed outcome snapshot diff in the same pull request and be explained in its body.\n- No new stored class value. No reader may decide anything from benchmark.compliance_class, conformance_class or summary.tpc_metrics.suppressed.\n- Paths, line numbers and counts in this plan were read on 2026-11-22 at develop 93f3360. Re-read before editing; report drift, do not guess.\n- AGENTS.md applies: linked worktree, one pull request per item, close at the merged pull request, heavy work only through make heavy-run, no live cloud run without owner approval in that task.\n- At a decision gate, follow the recorded default. If its stop condition is met, stop and report to the owner. Never substitute a different owner decision.\n- Read crr-00-corpus-rule-remediation-plan first: it holds the owner decisions, the rule table and the fault types (T1 to T5).",
